" A sample /SYSTEM/ETC/VI.RC -- copy it to VI.RC in this directory and edit.
" VI runs it at startup, one ex command to a line, so the mappings you
" want are there every session instead of being typed again. A line
" starting with " is a comment. Your own copy is never overwritten.

" leave insert mode without reaching for Escape
imap jk <Esc>
imap kj <Esc>

" write and quit from the home row
map ,w :w
map ,q :q

" Tab puts spaces to the next stop, never a tab character: the width,
" 1 to 16, for VI and PROG alike (typed in VI it is :set ts=2)
set ts=4
